     "text": "CLINICAL SUMMARY - Castillo PLC Clinic\nPatient: Tanya Stokes DOB: 09/01/1972 Sex: F MRN: 151516\n\nEncounters:\n2025-03-02 - Annual physical examination was performed. Blood pressure was recorded at 133/83 mmHg and weight was 201 pounds. Patient reported no significant complaints and appeared in generally good health. \nVital signs were within normal Physical examination showed no abnormalities. \n\n2024-05-01 - Visit for evaluation of a rash. Blood pressure was 117/82 mmHg and weight was 194 pounds. reported the rash had started approximately two weeks prior and was localized to the face and chest. The rash appeared erythematous and mildly pruritic. Given the appearance and location, it was suspected to be a flare of her known rosacea. Ivermectin topical 1% was prescribed to be applied twice daily to the affected areas. Patient was advised to follow up if symptoms persist or worsen. \n\n2023-07-01 - Visit for ongoing management of rosacea. Blood pressure was 118/74 mmHg and weight was 201 pounds. Patient reported her rosacea has been well controlled on ivermectin topical 1%, which she has been applying twice daily as prescribed. There were no new complaints or concerns.\n\nAssessment/Plan:\n• Rosacea Controlled on ivermectin topical 1%. Patient reports good adherence to the prescribed treatment and has experienced no recent flare-ups. She is advised to continue with the current treatment regimen and to monitor for any signs of worsening. \n\n• Exercise - Patient engages in running 3-4 times per week, which is consistent with her previously documented exercise habits. This regular physical activity contributes to her overall health and well-being.\n\n• Tobacco use - Patient is a former smoker, having smoked one pack per day since starting in 1995. She quit smoking on April 4, 2024. The patient has been honest and forthcoming about her smoking history.\n\n• Alcohol consumption - Patient reports consuming approximately 4 drinks per week, is within moderate limits.\n\nThe patient's overall health is stable. She is compliant with her medications and follows up as needed. There are no other significant findings from her recent encounters. She is encouraged to maintain her current healthy lifestyle and continue with regular medical follow-ups.\n\nDr. Jeremiah Davis\nFamily Medicine\nCastillo PLC Clinic\n"
